KZ3 patch 4030 (network pass 16): keyboard-and-mouse turn the valve and place the charge with the game's own code.
Root cause of a 7-minute stall at the Flooded Pyrrhus burning-gate valve (level 201, the RE notes s.14): the
valve (ValveJoystickController::Update 1.14 0x61AEB4, 1.00 0x606884) and the charge (ExplosiveLocationJoystickController,
target function 1.14 0x6126E4, 1.00 0x5FE0B4) read the RIGHT STICK's absolute angle while the grab actions 30/31
(GrabLeftHand/GrabRightHand; Standard and Alternate schemes: L1/R1, Modern: L2/R2) are held. The port already forces
profile byte 0xB6 (Motion Sensor Function) to 0 on a pad without gyro (kz3_sixaxis_filter), so that stick path is the
one in use. The mouse only fed the camera and the keys are digital, so there was no gesture a keyboard player could find.
Fix (an input mapping, default on; KZ3_MOUSE_STICK=0 off): libs/input/pad_assist.h + cellPad.c. While a post-hook of
those two controllers (port/spu glue: KZ3_HOOK_VALVE_ASSIST(0061AEB4), KZ3_HOOK_CHARGE_ASSIST(006126E4); they only
stamp the section here) ran in the last 250 ms, the mouse drives a virtual right stick (counts integrated, full travel
in the pointed direction above 0.25, so the valve's dead zone 0.29 and its x*x+y*y >= 0.25 test are cleared) and, while
Mouse1 is down, the pad button that the game's OWN action table (profile +0xE4 + 4*31, read through the same version
check as pad_actions_sync) gives GrabRightHand is pressed. A real stick or the right-stick keys win over the virtual
one. pad_mouse.c keeps a separate count for it (pad_mouse_stick_take), so mouse look is not affected. Mouse look does not
fire on a valve: kz3_mouse_look_pre acts on the soldier's on-foot SetViewAngles call (lr 0x0069B120) and the mounted-gun
look update only. Test input: KZ3_MOUSE_STICK_FEED="T:dx,dy*SECONDS ..." (counts per second into the virtual stick on the pad script clock).
Log lines: "[mousestick] section on/off", "[assist] valve section: entity=... n= disable= dir=
handlimit=", "[assist] valve n= hand= grab=" (each 5 % of travel), "[assist] charge section: ... windows= centres=". Host test: tools/smoke/test_motion_assist.sh.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 153): cellPad.c and pad_mouse.c context follows v0.19 plus 2099's pad_mouse part (look accumulator); hunks unchanged.

